d":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the dedup behaviour when the material fingerprint cannot be read: fail-closed (treat unknown material as a distinct key / fresh job) rather than collapsing to the old material-blind key, so a read failure cannot silently reintroduce the stale-dedup window.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.62,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'returns None on a read failure, which keeps the old key behaviour for that call'","Root cause W1: material absent from key causes post-edit start to dedup to pre-edit run","ABSENCE: plan does not state consumer tolerance when the fingerprint is unavailable — None re-opens the stale window rather than failing closed (treating unknown material as distinct)"],"finding":"The fingerprint helper 'returns None on a read failure, which keeps the old key behaviour for that call' — this silently reintroduces the exact stale-dedup window the plan fixes: under a transient fingerprint read failure, a post-edit start and the pre-edit in-flight run collapse to the same singleflight key again, so the author's re-review attaches to the stale run.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3f4a234cd9f0c407","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1: '_plan_review_variant ... returns None on a read failure, which keeps the old key behaviour'","norm_id":"nf3ae23e288b49f0c","priority":0.33,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A fingerprint read fails transiently during a re-review after an edit; the second start dedups to the stale in-flight run and the author again sees pre-edit findings — the reported symptom recurs"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"On fingerprint read failure, incorporate a unique/degraded token into the variant so the start is treated as new material rather than matching an in-flight run; document the retryable disposition.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify and test the dedup behaviour when `current_material_fingerprint` returns None: justify fail-open vs. fail-closed (treat unknown material as a distinct/fresh key, matching retry.py's documented fail-closed convention) and add an AC covering the read-failure path.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.37,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 1: 'returns None on a read failure, which keeps the old key behaviour for that call.'","`compute_key` hashes the `variant` string as-is (src/rebar/_mcp_inflight.py:87) — two None-fingerprint variants are byte-identical and dedup together.","The identical read fails CLOSED elsewhere in plan review: tests/unit/test_plan_review_retry.py:367 'current_material_fingerprint returns None on a read error (documented fail-closed) ... The gate must treat unknown as STALE.'","No acceptance criterion exercises the None/read-failure path; the behaviour is asserted only in prose."],"finding":"The fallback for the failed fingerprint sub-step (the light `current_material_fingerprint` read returning None) is under-specified and chosen fail-OPEN without justification: substituting `fp=None` into `material={fp}` yields a constant variant for every failed read, so two `review_plan_start` calls straddling an edit that both hit a read failure will share one dedup key and attach to the pre-edit run — reproducing the exact stale-review symptom the ticket fixes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4e0d99d11ef63784","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan' step 1 (`_plan_review_variant`); Acceptance criteria","norm_id":"nb5348ea9ea4c5682","priority":0.33,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A transient store/git read error during the post-edit window makes the fingerprint uncomputable for both the in-flight run's start and the author's re-review start; both get `material=None` and dedup, so the edited plan is never reviewed through the new start.","An archived/deleted-then-recreated child causing a None light read while a review is in flight."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"On a None fingerprint, encode a unique/unknown sentinel into the variant (e.g. a per-call nonce or `material=unknown:<uuid>`) so an uncomputable read forces a fresh job rather than sharing one, consistent with retry.py's STALE-on-None handling; add an AC asserting two starts with a None fingerprint do NOT dedup.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Log (or metric) the `current_material_fingerprint` read-failure/None path so a fallback to the material-less dedup key is observable, and state the residual stale-dedup risk window of that fallback.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 1: 'returns None on a read failure, which keeps the old key behaviour for that call'","The 'old key behaviour' is exactly the W1 defect this ticket fixes; under a transient read failure the fix is silently disabled","No log/metric/trace is mentioned for the None path, so the silent fallback is unobservable to operators"],"finding":"The new fingerprint read (`current_material_fingerprint`) returns None on a read failure, silently reverting the dedup key to the pre-fix (buggy) `source=`-only variant for that call, with no log/metric so operators cannot see when the fallback — and thus the stale-material dedup window — re-activates.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f35aff6353e937bed","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1 ('returns None on a read failure, which keeps the old key behaviour for that call')","norm_id":"n9ed729792cec0d4b","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A transient store read error occurs during a start; the variant loses the material dimension and a post-edit start can dedup onto a pre-edit run — reproducing the original symptom with no diagnostic trail"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In `_plan_review_variant`, emit a warning-level log when the fingerprint read returns None (variant falling back to `source=`-only), and note in the plan that this reopens the W1 window for the duration of the transient read failure.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"2d970dc2efcbc25b","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["52943bbb44fe9393",5716],"description_boxes":["7879981d4f226a8f",0],"file_impact":["aaf5ac83e1b3c67c",2],"ticket_id":["5f12697c8780f552",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":427352,"cache_write_tokens":175924,"claim_path":"no-llm/